## Routing (the `milo` arm)

- Tiers chosen: fast 35, mid 41, frontier 41
- Tier agreement with the label: 82.1% (n=117)
- Sticky (inherited) decisions: 0
- Jev latency: mean 455 ms, p95 768 ms (n=117)
- Routing overhead (routed TTFB minus the same model called directly): p50 628 ms, p95 2417 ms (n=114)
- Bad downgrades (routed cheaper than frontier, failed, frontier passed): 9 of 112
- Missed savings (routed to frontier, fast passed): 7 of 112

## Best-of-5 sampling on `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (fast tier, prompt framings varied)

- Samples: 600 drawn over 120 examples; 596 succeeded, 596 graded, 596 ranked by Jev (0 ranking failures)
- Random pick (mean per-sample pass rate): 66.9%
- Coverage (some sample passes): 83.3% — the ceiling any selector could reach
- Jev as verifier: AUROC 0.907 on its quality score, 0.900 on its correctness probability (0.5 is chance)
- Where samples disagree (43 examples): Jev's pick passed 88.4% of the time, a random pick 54.5%, the oracle 100%
- Jev ranking latency: mean 500 ms per sample, charged at $0.00002 per call

